tage.\n\nI should also consider things like local language processing, which might be more accurate for the user's specific language. Maybe things like voice commands without internet", "outputSample": "<think>\nOkay, the user is asking for a list of 25 distinct things that on-device AI can do on a phone that a cloud model cannot. Let me start by understanding the difference between on-device AI and c", "provenance": {"definitions": "prefill tok/s = prompt_tokens / (prompt_eval_end_ms - inference_start_ms) * 1000. The window opens before the runner tokenizes the prompt (TextLLMRunner::generate sets inference_start_ms, then encodes), so prefill includes tokenization.\nTTFT ms = first_token_ms - inference_start_ms = the same window (first_token_ms is taken when prefill returns, before the first token is decoded to text).\ndecode tok/s = generated_tokens / (inference_end_ms - prompt_eval_end_ms) * 1000, generated_tokens = tokens of the decode loop; the reply has one more token, the one prefill sampled.\ncold = one generation in a fresh llama_main process (no --warmup). warm = llama_main --warmup: one unmeasured generation of the same prompt and max_new_tokens in the same process, stats and KV position reset, the second generation measured.\nClock: integer milliseconds (extension/llm/runner/util.h time_in_ms).", "recipe": "Qwen3-4B-ET1.5.1-xnnpack-8da4w-emb8-ctx2048.recipe.json", "recipeSha256": "937aeb90071174157a165d07a067e5e50febfef815f875479d75620a58487a47", "recipeAlias": "et1.5.1-xnnpack-8da4w-g128-emb8", "exporter": "extension/llm/export/export_llm (examples/models/qwen3/config/qwen3_xnnpack_q8da4w.yaml)", "modelProvenance": "own export with the ExecuTorch tag's own exporter (recipe.json beside the .pte); not a published artifact", "promptFile": "Qwen3-4B-ET1.5.1-xnnpack-8da4w-emb8-ctx2048.prompts/long-context-1024-gen256.chat.txt", "promptSha256": "360771899cd15f27bcedd5911f5c7f6775ccc15a092e2d133ec29cd83c90baf2", "tokenizer": "tokenizer.json", "tokenizerSha256"